  "details": "Repro steps of one of problematic behaviours:\n1. Launch CreatorCompanion from start menu of Windows\n2. Launch CreatorCompanion again. Then a window of secound instance appears.\n3. Do \"new project\" on second instance. The view changes to \"Please Wait...\" appearance.\n4. Wait a moment. Then Unity opens up. (Maybe creating a project is completed on Unity side.)\n5. Second instance stick on \"Please Wait...\" view.\n6. Kill the second instance (by Alt-F4 for instance)\n7. Launch CreatorCompanion again. you see the project list is not updated.\nI think it should be prevented to launch multiple instances as Unity Hub does.",
